Do you know if your hands or some other part of your body is asleep? When a limb is asleep, it feels numb and can be quite uncomfortable. This happens when the blood supply to a particular area of the body is temporarily interrupted or reduced. As a result, the nerve endings in that area do not receive enough oxygen and nutrients, leading to the sensation of numbness, tingling, or a lack of sensation. Once the blood flow is restored to normal, the feeling in the affected body part usually returns quickly, and the uncomfortable sensations gradually fade away.
